g pulses and flashes repeatedly, without necessarily requiring a fixed pattern.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R003\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every request, a pulse and a flash must occur at some later step or steps; their order is not fixed.\",\n        \"For every request, both a pulse and a flash are required after it, possibly including the same step as the request.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R004\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"If a stop occurs, then before that stop there must have been at least one pulse and at least one flash.\",\n        \"No stop may occur until both a pulse and a flash have occurred.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R005\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every request, before the next stop after that request, both a pulse and a flash must occur.\",\n        \"If there is no next stop, the pulse and flash are still required eventually, because the request creates an obligation.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R006\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"There is some step t such that the signal and the indicator are both active at t and at t plus one.\",\n        \"Both the signal and the indicator must be simultaneously active for a continuous run of at least two steps at some point.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R007\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"The signal becomes active at some future step and the indicator becomes active at some future step, not necessarily the same step.\",\n        \"Both the signal and the indicator must eventually be active, without any requirement that they remain active.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R008\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"From some step onward, the signal and the indicator are active and remain active until a release occurs.\",\n        \"If no release occurs, then from that eventual point the signal and the indicator remain active forever.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R009\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"There exists a pulse and a flash that occur before some completion event.\",\n        \"A pulse and a flash must occur at some point, and a completion must occur later than them.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R010\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"If a start occurs, then before the next finish after that start, both a pulse and a flash must occur.\",\n        \"If no finish occurs after the start, the pulse and flash are still eventually required by the start.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R011\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"There is a step where a pulse occurs and the immediately next step where a flash occurs, and separately there is a step where a click occurs and the immediately next step where a mark appears.\",\n        \"The pulse-flash pair and the click-mark pair may occur at different times, but each pair must be consecutive.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R012\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Infinitely often, the signal and the indicator are both active for two consecutive steps.\",\n        \"The requirement is that active periods of the signal and indicator keep recurring and each such period lasts at least two consecutive steps.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R013\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every pulse, a flash must occur at some strictly later step.\",\n        \"For every pulse, a flash must occur after it, possibly immediately after, but not necessarily on the same step.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R014\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"If a pulse occurs at the current step, then a flash must occur at some future step.\",\n        \"If a pulse occurs now, a flash must occur immediately after, for example at the next step.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R015\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"There exists at least one pulse followed later by at least one flash.\",\n        \"At least one pulse-flash sequence occurs, while other pulses may be unconstrained.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R016\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every pulse, after that pulse the indicator becomes on and remains on forever.\",\n        \"For every pulse, the indicator must be on from the pulse step or the next step onward and never turn off.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R017\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"At least one stop occurs, and every pulse before the first stop must have some later flash, even if that flash occurs after the stop.\",\n        \"The obligation applies only to pulses in the prefix before the first stop, but their flash fulfillment is not limited to that prefix.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R018\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every pulse, there is a later flash, and after that flash there is a strictly later chime.\",\n        \"Each pulse must be followed by a flash-chime sequence, with the chime occurring at a step after the flash.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R019\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"No pulse may have a flash at any strictly later step.\",\n        \"If a pulse occurs, then a flash must never occur afterward, though a flash before the pulse may be allowed.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R020\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every pulse, before the next stop after that pulse, a flash must occur, and the flash step must not also be a stop.\",\n        \"If there is no subsequent stop, the pulse still requires a flash eventually, but the stop-related constraint is vacuous.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R021\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever pulses occur on two consecutive steps, a flash must occur at some later step after that pair.\",\n        \"The obligation is triggered only by consecutive-pulse patterns, not by isolated pulses.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R022\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"There exists a step N such that every pulse at or after N is followed by a flash at a later step.\",\n        \"Before N, pulses may be unfulfilled; after N, the pulse-to-flash rule holds permanently.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R023\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Infinitely often, a pulse occurs and is followed later by a flash.\",\n        \"The pulse-flash sequence must repeat without end, though the spacing between occurrences is not fixed.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R024\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"At the first activation step, every pulse from that step onward must be followed by a flash at a later step.\",\n        \"Pulses before activation are unconstrained, but activation starts a permanent pulse-to-flash obligation.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R025\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Every request must be accompanied or followed by an active response.\",\n        \"Every request requires an active response, possibly at the same step or at a later step.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R026\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"If a request occurs at the initial step, then an active response must occur at some later step.\",\n        \"If a request occurs at the initial step, then an active response must occur immediately, possibly at the same or next step.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R027\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"There exists at least one step where a request occurs and the response is active at that step.\",\n        \"There exists at least one request that is followed by an active response.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R028\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Infinitely often, a request occurs together with an active response.\",\n        \"The pattern of request with active response must keep recurring without end.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R029\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"There exists a step N such that from N onward, every request has an active response.\",\n        \"Eventually, no request may occur without an active response.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R030\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"A release must occur, and before that release every request requires an active response.\",\n        \"After the release, requests no longer require an active response.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R031\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"If no release occurs, then every request forever requires an active response.\",\n        \"Once a release occurs, the request-response requirement ends; release is optional.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R032\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Starting at the first release step, every later request requires an active response.\",\n        \"Requests before the first release are unconstrained, but requests at or after the first release are obligated.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R033\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every request, the response becomes active at some point and then remains active forever.\",\n        \"Each request triggers a permanent active response, possibly starting at the request step or later.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R034\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every request, the response must remain active until a later release, and at least one release must occur.\",\n        \"Each request creates a continuous active-response obligation ending at a mandatory release.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R035\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"If a request occurs at the next step, then an active response must occur at some later step.\",\n        \"If a request occurs at the next step, then an active response must occur immediately, possibly at that next step or the step after it.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R036\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Any request that occurs while the response is permitted must have an active response later.\",\n        \"Only requests made during permitted states create an active-response obligation; other requests are unconstrained.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R037\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever a pulse occurs, a flash must occur at the same step or at a later step.\",\n        \"There exists a pulse that is followed by a flash, possibly on the same step.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R038\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever a pulse occurs, the light must be on at that same step.\",\n        \"At least one pulse must coincide with the light being on.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R039\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever a pulse occurs, a flash must occur exactly at the next step.\",\n        \"There exists a pulse followed immediately by a flash on the next step.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R040\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever a pulse occurs, the light must be on from that step onward and remain on forever.\",\n        \"A pulse triggers permanent light-on beginning at the pulse step.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R041\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever a pulse occurs, the light must be on until a release occurs, and a release is required.\",\n        \"A pulse creates a light-on obligation that ends only at a mandatory later release.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R042\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever a pulse occurs, the light must stay on until a release; if no release occurs, the light stays on forever.\",\n        \"A pulse creates a liveness obligation for the light to remain on through the first subsequent release, if any.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R043\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every pulse, there must be a first release at or after that pulse, and at that release step the light must be on.\",\n        \"The pulse does not require the light to stay on continuously, only to be on at the first relevant release.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R044\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every pulse, before any flash at or after that pulse, a release must occur; then a flash must occur at or after that release.\",\n        \"The required order is pulse, then release, then flash, with no flash before the release.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R045\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever a pulse occurs while the enable state holds, a flash must occur at that step or later.\",\n        \"Only enabled pulses create a flash obligation; pulses while disabled are unconstrained.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R046\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For any pulse occurring before the first stop, a flash must occur at the pulse step or later.\",\n        \"The flash obligation is triggered by pre-stop pulses, but the flash itself is not explicitly restricted to occur before the stop.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R047\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"At the current step, neither the first indicator nor the second indicator is active.\",\n        \"Both indicators must be inactive now, with no constraint on later steps.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R048\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"At every step, neither the first indicator nor the second indicator is active.\",\n        \"Both indicators must remain inactive forever.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R049\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"There exists at least one step where neither the first indicator nor the second indicator is active.\",\n        \"At some future time, both indicators must be inactive simultaneously.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R050\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"There are infinitely many steps where neither the first indicator nor the second indicator is active.\",\n        \"The state in which both indicators are inactive must recur forever.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R051\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"There exists a step N such that from N onward, neither indicator is active.\",\n        \"Eventually, both indicators become permanently inactive.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R052\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"A release must occur, and before that release neither indicator may be active.\",\n        \"After the release, the indicators may become active.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R053\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Neither indicator may be active until a release occurs; if no release occurs, they remain inactive forever.\",\n        \"If a release occurs, the inactivity requirement holds up to that release, and release is optional.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R054\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"At every step where the gate is open, neither indicator is active.\",\n        \"The open gate forbids active indicators at the same step.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R055\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every pulse at step t, neither indicator is active at step t plus one.\",\n        \"Each pulse triggers a one-step inactive period for both indicators immediately afterward.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R056\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every pulse at step t, there exists some step t prime greater than or equal to t where neither indicator is active.\",\n        \"The inactive step may be the pulse step itself or any later step.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R057\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every pulse at step t, a release must occur at some step t prime greater than or equal to t, and neither indicator may be active until that release.\",\n        \"Each pulse creates a mandatory release and an inactivity period lasting until that release.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R058\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"There exists a step where a check occurs and neither indicator is active.\",\n        \"At least one check must coincide with both indicators being inactive.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R059\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Every request must be followed by at least one of a pulse or a flash.\",\n        \"A request may be answered by a pulse, by a flash, or by both, but at least one must occur.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R060\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every request at step t, either a pulse or a flash occurs at step t plus one.\",\n        \"The response must occur exactly on the next step, not merely later.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R061\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every request, a pulse or a flash must occur immediately, possibly at the same step, and exactly one of them must occur.\",\n        \"For every request, the immediate next step must contain either a pulse or a flash, but not both.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R062\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every request at step t, either a pulse occurs at t plus one and a flash occurs at t plus two, or a flash occurs at t plus one and a pulse occurs at t plus two.\",\n        \"Each request starts a two-step response consisting of one pulse and one flash in either order.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R063\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every request, either the first signal or the second signal must remain active until a later release, and a release must eventually occur.\",\n        \"A request chooses one of the two signals to hold active until a mandatory release ends the obligation.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R064\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every request, either the first signal or the second signal must remain active until a release; if no release occurs, it remains active forever.\",\n        \"The active-signal obligation ends only if a release occurs, but release is optional.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R065\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"A stop must eventually occur, and before that stop every request must receive an immediate pulse or flash.\",\n        \"The immediate-response requirement applies until the first stop, and the stop is mandatory.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R066\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"If no stop occurs, then every request forever requires an immediate pulse or flash.\",\n        \"If a stop occurs, the immediate-response requirement ends at that stop, but the stop is not required.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R067\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every request, before the next stop after it, a pulse or a flash must occur.\",\n        \"If there is no next stop, the pulse or flash is still eventually required by the request.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R068\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"From some relevant point, the state remains active until a release occurs.\",\n        \"If no release occurs, the state remains active forever.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R069\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every request at step t, the state must remain active from t or a later step until a release occurs.\",\n        \"Each request creates an active-state obligation that ends at a release, possibly requiring eventual release.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R070\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"There exists a step N such that from N onward the state remains active until a release occurs.\",\n        \"Before N the state may be inactive; after N it becomes active and stays active until release.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R071\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"At every step, the state must be active and remain active until a release occurs.\",\n        \"The obligation to stay active until release holds globally from every step, implying permanent activity if no release occurs.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R072\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"The state remains active and the indicator remains lit until a release occurs.\",\n        \"If no release occurs, the state remains active and the indicator remains lit forever.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R073\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"The state remains active until the first of a release or a cancellation occurs.\",\n        \"Either a release or a cancellation ends the active-state obligation; neither event is explicitly required.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R074\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"The state remains active until a release occurs at a step when the indicator is lit.\",\n        \"The terminating release must coincide with the indicator being lit.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R075\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"The state remains active until a point from which the indicator stays lit forever.\",\n        \"Permanent illumination of the indicator ends the active-state obligation.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R076\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"For every request at step t, the state must remain active starting at step t plus one until a release occurs.\",\n        \"The request itself does not require the state to be active at the request step, only from the next step onward.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R077\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Before the first release, every pulse must be followed by a flash exactly at the next step.\",\n        \"After the release occurs, the pulse-to-next-step-flash obligation no longer applies.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R078\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"The first state remains active until a handoff occurs; after the handoff, the second state remains active until a release, and that release must eventually occur.\",\n        \"The behavior is a two-phase sequence: first-state active, handoff, second-state active, mandatory release.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R079\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"A handoff must eventually occur, with the first state active before it; from the handoff onward, the second state remains active until a release occurs.\",\n        \"The handoff is mandatory, the second state obligation starts at the handoff, and a release eventually ends it.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R080\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever a pulse occurs, a flash must occur at some strictly later step.\",\n        \"There exists a pulse that is followed later by a flash.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R081\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever a pulse occurs at step t, the light is on for every step after t and remains on forever.\",\n        \"A pulse triggers permanent light-on starting at the next step.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R082\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever a pulse occurs, there is some later step from which the light becomes on and remains on forever.\",\n        \"The light may fluctuate before settling, but after the pulse it eventually enters a permanently on state.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R083\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever a pulse occurs, a flash occurs later, and then a chime occurs later than that flash.\",\n        \"The required order is pulse, then flash, then chime.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R084\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever a pulse occurs at step t, a flash occurs at some later step t prime, and no pulse occurs between t and t prime.\",\n        \"The required flash must come before any subsequent pulse.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R085\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever a pulse occurs at step t, a flash occurs at some later step t prime, and no pause state holds between t and t prime.\",\n        \"The required flash must occur before any pause after the pulse.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R086\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever a pulse occurs, the first later release occurs while the light is on.\",\n        \"The light need not remain on continuously, but it must be on at the next release after the pulse.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"R087\",\n      \"comments\": \"Open interpretation only.\",\n      \"interpretations\": [\n        \"Whenever a pulse occurs while the enable state holds, a flas