es before activation unconstrained.\n\nR025: \"Requests require an active response.\" props a request, b response active. Interpretations:\n1. Every request must be accompanied/answered by response active at some later step.\n2. Every request requires response active immediately (same step or next). Need include.\n\nR026: \"A request at the starting step requires an active response.\" props a,b. Interpretations:\n1. If request occurs at initial step, response must be active later.\n2. If request occurs at initial step, response must be active at same/next step. Need scope only initial.\n\nR027: \"There must be a request with an active response.\" props a,b. Interpretations:\n1. There exists a step where request occurs and response is active (possibly same step).\n2. There exists a request and, at some later step, active response.\n\nR028: \"Requests with an active response must keep occurring.\" props a,b. Interpretations:\n1. Infinitely often, a request occurs together with active response.\n2. The pattern request+active response repeats indefinitely.\n\nR029: \"Eventually, requests must always have an active response.\" props a,b. Interpretations:\n1. From some step onward, every request has active response (same/later).\n2. There is a point after which no request occurs without active response.\n\nR030: \"Requests require an active response until a release occurs, and a release must occur.\" props a,b,c release. Interpretations:\n1. A release occurs; before that release, every request requires active response.\n2. After release, requests no longer require active response; release is mandatory.\n\nR031: \"Requests require an active response unless and until a release occurs.\" props a,b,c. Interpretations:\n1. If no release occurs, all requests require active response forever.\n2. Once release occurs, obligation ends; release optional.\n\nR032: \"From the first release onward, requests require an active response.\" props a,b,c. Interpretations:\n1. Starting at first release step N, every request at t>=N requires active response.\n2. Before first release, requests unconstrained; after release, obligation begins.\n\nR033: \"Every request requires a response that remains active forever.\" props a,b. Interpretations:\n1. For every request, response becomes active at some point and then remains active permanently.\n2. Each request triggers permanent active response, possibly starting same/next step.\n\nR034: \"Every request requires the response to stay active until a release, which must occur.\" props a,b,c. Interpretations:\n1. For every request, response stays active until a later release; at least one release occurs.\n2. Release mandatory; response active continuously from request to release.\n\nR035: \"A request at the next step requires an active response.\" props a,b. Interpretations:\n1. If request occurs at step 1 (next step), response must be active later.\n2. If request occurs at step 1, response active at same/next step. Need maybe \"next step\" relative to now.\n\nR036: \"Requests made while the response is permitted require an active response.\" props a,b,c permitted. Interpretations:\n1. Any request at a step where response is permitted must have active response later.\n2. Only requests in permitted state are obligated; requests when not permitted unconstrained.\n\nR037: \"A pulse is to be followed by a flash, possibly at the same step.\" props a,b. Interpretations:\n1. There exists a pulse with a flash at same or later step.\n2. If pulse occurs, a flash occurs at same step or after. Need scope? \"A pulse\" could be any pulse? Maybe generic. Include universal/existential.\n\nR038: \"A pulse requires the light to be on at that step.\" props a,b. Interpretations:\n1. Whenever pulse occurs, light is on at same step.\n2. At least one pulse must coincide with light on. Need likely universal.\n\nR039: \"A pulse is to have a flash at the next step.\" props a,b. Interpretations:\n1. Whenever pulse occurs, flash occurs exactly one step later.\n2. There exists a pulse followed immediately next step by flash. Need generic.\n\nR040: \"A pulse requires the light to stay on from that step onward.\" props a,b. Interpretations:\n1. Whenever pulse occurs, light is on at pulse step and remains on forever.\n2. Pulse triggers permanent light-on from that step.\n\nR041: \"A pulse calls for the light to be on until a release occurs, with a release required.\" props a,b,c. Interpretations:\n1. Whenever pulse occurs, light must be on until some later release; release mandatory.\n2. The obligation may start at pulse step or next; release ends it.\n\nR042: \"A pulse calls for the light to stay on until a release, or forever if no release comes.\" props a,b,c. Interpretations:\n1. Whenever pulse occurs, light remains on until first release after it; if no release, remains on forever.\n2. Release optional; obligation is liveness until release.\n\nR043: \"A pulse calls for the light to be on at the first release at or after that pulse, and that release must occur.\" props a,b,c. Interpretations:\n1. For each pulse, there is a release at or after it, and at that first release step light is on.\n2. Release mandatory; only light at release step required, not continuous.\n\nR044: \"A pulse calls for a release before any flash from that step onward, and a flash at or after the release.\" props a,b,c. Interpretations:\n1. For each pulse, before any flash at/after pulse, a release must occur; then a flash occurs at/after that release.\n2. Sequence: pulse -> release -> flash; no flash before release.\n\nR045: \"A pulse while enabled calls for a flash at that step or later.\" props a,b,c enable. Interpretations:\n1. Whenever pulse occurs while enable state holds, a flash occurs at same or later step.\n2. Only enabled pulses trigger flash obligation; disabled pulses unconstrained.\n\nR046: \"Before the first stop, a pulse calls for a flash at that step or later.\" props a,b,c stop. Interpretations:\n1. For any pulse occurring before first stop, a flash occurs at same or later step (possibly after stop?). Wording \"before first stop, a pulse calls\" maybe flash at or later not necessarily before stop. Need include.\n2. If pulse before first stop, flash obligation arises; flash may occur after stop unless constrained.\n\nR047: \"The first and second indicators must not be active now.\" props a,b. Interpretations:\n1. At current/initial step, neither first nor second indicator is active.\n2. Both indicators must be inactive at now; later unconstrained.\n\nR048: \"The first and second indicators must never be active.\" props a,b. Interpretations:\n1. At all steps, neither indicator is active.\n2. Both indicators remain inactive forever.\n\nR049: \"At some point, the first and second indicators must not be active.\" props a,b. Interpretations:\n1. There exists a step where both are inactive.\n2. At some future time, neither first nor second indicator is active.\n\nR050: \"Infinitely often, the first and second indicators must not be active.\" props a,b. Interpretations:\n1. There are infinitely many steps where both indicators are inactive.\n2. The inactive state recurs forever.\n\nR051: \"From some point onward, the first and second indicators must not be active.\" props a,b. Interpretations:\n1. There exists N such that for all t>=N, both indicators inactive.\n2. Eventually both indicators become permanently inactive.\n\nR052: \"The first and second indicators must not be active until a release occurs, and a release must occur.\" props a,b,c. Interpretations:\n1. Before the first release, both indicators inactive; release eventually occurs.\n2. After release, indicators may become active.\n\nR053: \"The first and second indicators must not be active until a release occurs; release is optional.\" props a,b,c. Interpretations:\n1. Both inactive until some release; if no release occurs, they remain inactive forever.\n2. If release occurs, inactivity required up to that release ste