h.\" props a,b,c. Interpretations:\n1. Every request at t is answered at same step by exactly one of pulse or flash.\n2. \"At once\" could mean immediately next step? Need include: same step or immediate next, exclusive.\n\nR062: \"Every request starts a pulse-then-flash or flash-then-pulse response, with the two events on consecutive steps.\" props a,b,c. Interpretations:\n1. For every request at t, either pulse at t+1 and flash at t+2, or flash at t+1 and pulse at t+2.\n2. Response order may be either, events consecutive after request.\n\nR063: \"A request requires the first or second signal to stay active until a release, which must eventually occur.\" props a,b first signal,c second signal,d release. Interpretations:\n1. For every request, either first or second signal remains active until some later release; release mandatory.\n2. The active signal may be chosen per request; obligation ends at release.\n\nR064: \"A request requires the first or second signal to remain active unless released; release is optional.\" props a,b,c,d. Interpretations:\n1. For every request, one of the signals stays active until a release; if no release, stays active forever.\n2. Release optional; before release, active signal required.\n\nR065: \"Until a stop occurs, requests must receive an immediate pulse or flash; a stop must eventually occur.\" props a,b,c,d. Interpretations:\n1. A stop occurs; before that stop, every request is answered immediately by pulse or flash.\n2. After stop, immediate response requirement ends.\n\nR066: \"Unless a stop occurs, requests must receive an immediate pulse or flash; a stop is not required.\" props a,b,c,d. Interpretations:\n1. If no stop occurs, all requests forever require immediate pulse/flash.\n2. If stop occurs, requirement ends at stop; stop optional.\n\nR067: \"Requests must receive a pulse or flash before the next stop.\" props a,b,c,d. Interpretations:\n1. For every request, before the next stop after it, pulse or flash occurs.\n2. If 